<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  migears/xml-pages — a full-featured example
  ==================================================================

  This file covers every declarative construct xml-pages supports. It can be
  compiled and rendered directly, and also serves as a reference for writing
  your own pages.

  Structural conventions (see README "XML writing notes"):
    · The element name is the node type: text / heading / link / if / each / form / table / component
    · Fields go in attributes, e.g. <heading level="2">, <link href="...">
    · A leaf element's own text is its text field; leading and trailing
      whitespace is trimmed
    · Container children: <then>/<else>, <body>, <fields>, <columns>, <content>, <data>

  Compile (the output lands in examples/views/, on the same template search
  path as the layout):
      php bin/xml-pages compile examples/full-featured.page.xml examples/views

  Render (built-in components live in the package components/, this example's
  custom component in examples/components/):
      $tpl = new Template(__DIR__ . '/examples/views');
      $tpl->addPath(__DIR__ . '/components');            // built-in: card / button / alert / badge
      $tpl->addPath(__DIR__ . '/examples/components');   // custom: my-card
      echo $tpl->render('full-featured', $data);

  Note: layout and body are mutually exclusive, so they cannot be demonstrated
  in the same file. The standalone (layout-less) page form is commented out at
  the end of the file.
-->
<page title="User management · Full-featured example" layout="layout/main">
    <sections>
        <section name="content">

            <!-- ======================================================
                 1. heading / text / link —— titles, text and links
                 ====================================================== -->

            <!-- heading: level is optional (default 1), valid range 1-6 -->
            <heading>Page content</heading>
            <heading level="2">1. Titles, text and links</heading>
            <heading level="3">Third-level heading</heading>

            <!-- text: the element's own text is the content; literal parts are
                 emitted as written and interpolations are auto-escaped -->
            <text>This is a plain paragraph.</text>
            <text>Hello, {{ user.name }}! You have {{ user.messageCount }} unread messages.</text>

            <!-- HTML that must be emitted as written is wrapped in CDATA -->
            <text><![CDATA[<strong>bold</strong>, <em>italic</em> — tags are emitted as written.]]></text>

            <!-- XML entities: &lt; &gt; &amp; stand for < > & -->
            <text>Comparison: a &lt; b, b &gt; a, and logical a &amp;&amp; b.</text>

            <!-- Multi-line text: internal line breaks are kept, leading and
                 trailing whitespace is trimmed -->
            <text>first line
second line</text>

            <!-- link: href is required, the element text is the link label;
                 target is optional; attribute values support interpolation too -->
            <link href="/users/{{ user.id }}/edit">Edit current user</link>
            <link href="https://example.com/docs" target="_blank">Open the docs in a new window</link>

            <!-- ======================================================
                 2. if —— conditional display
                 when is required; <then> is required, <else> optional; a !
                 prefix negates
                 ====================================================== -->

            <heading level="2">2. Conditional display</heading>

            <if when="user.loggedIn">
                <then>
                    <text>Welcome back, {{ user.name }}.</text>
                </then>
                <else>
                    <text>Please log in first.</text>
                </else>
            </if>

            <!-- Negation: no escaping needed for ! in XML attributes -->
            <if when="!user.hidden">
                <then>
                    <text>This user's profile is visible to visitors.</text>
                </then>
            </if>

            <!-- Multi-segment paths work as conditions too:
                 form.errors.email -> $form['errors']['email'] -->
            <if when="form.errors.email">
                <then>
                    <text>Email error: {{ form.errors.email }}</text>
                </then>
            </if>

            <!-- ======================================================
                 3. each —— looping over a list
                 items is required; <body> is required; as defaults to item;
                 index is optional
                 ====================================================== -->

            <heading level="2">3. Loops</heading>

            <!-- Index variable: index yields the array key (0-based),
                 and {{ i }} is $i -->
            <each items="users" as="member" index="i">
                <body>
                    <text>{{ i }}. {{ member.name }} ({{ member.email }})</text>
                </body>
            </each>

            <!-- Nested each: the inner items may reference an outer variable,
                 e.g. group.members -->
            <each items="groups" as="group">
                <body>
                    <heading level="4">{{ group.name }}</heading>
                    <each items="group.members" as="member">
                        <body>
                            <text>· {{ member.name }}</text>
                        </body>
                    </each>
                </body>
            </each>

            <!-- if works inside a loop body too -->
            <each items="users" as="member">
                <body>
                    <if when="member.active">
                        <then>
                            <text>{{ member.name }} is enabled</text>
                        </then>
                        <else>
                            <text>{{ member.name }} is disabled</text>
                        </else>
                    </if>
                </body>
            </each>

            <!-- ======================================================
                 4. table —— tables
                 items is required; <columns> is required; as defaults to row;
                 empty is optional. Columns: label is required, and pop and
                 <content> are mutually exclusive
                 ====================================================== -->

            <heading level="2">4. Tables</heading>

            <table items="users" as="row" empty="No data">
                <columns>
                    <!-- pop: the server renders data into the cell,
                         written as {{ row.field }} -->
                    <column label="ID" pop="{{ row.id }}"/>
                    <column label="Name" pop="{{ row.name }}"/>
                    <column label="Email" pop="{{ row.email }}"/>
                    <!-- content: a node tree in the row's scope, may reference
                         row.* -->
                    <column label="Actions">
                        <content>
                            <link href="/users/{{ row.id }}/edit">Edit</link>
                        </content>
                    </column>
                </columns>
            </table>

            <!-- ======================================================
                 5. form + field —— forms
                 action is required; method defaults to post; <fields> is
                 required. input: text / password / email / number / textarea
                        / select / checkbox / hidden / submit
                 ====================================================== -->

            <heading level="2">5. Forms</heading>

            <form action="/users/save" method="post">
                <fields>
                    <!-- value binds a path, required is a boolean, placeholder
                         is for single-line inputs only -->
                    <field name="name" label="Name" input="text" value="user.name"
                           required="true" placeholder="Enter name"/>
                    <field name="password" label="Password" input="password" required="true"/>
                    <field name="email" label="Email" input="email" value="user.email"/>
                    <field name="age" label="Age" input="number" value="user.age"/>

                    <!-- textarea: rows defaults to 4 -->
                    <field name="bio" label="About" input="textarea" rows="6" value="user.bio"/>

                    <!-- select: <options> is required, and value binding is not
                         accepted -->
                    <field name="role" label="Role" input="select">
                        <options>
                            <option value="admin">Admin</option>
                            <option value="editor">Editor</option>
                            <option value="user">Standard user</option>
                        </options>
                    </field>

                    <!-- checkbox: checked binds a path; a truthy value emits
                         checked -->
                    <field name="active" label="Enabled" input="checkbox" checked="user.active"/>

                    <!-- hidden: no label is rendered -->
                    <field name="csrf" label="CSRF token" input="hidden" value="form.csrf"/>

                    <!-- submit: the label is the button text -->
                    <field name="submit" label="Save" input="submit"/>
                </fields>
            </form>

            <!-- method may be omitted (defaults to post), or set explicitly to
                 get -->
            <form action="/users/search" method="get">
                <fields>
                    <field name="q" label="Keyword" input="text" placeholder="Name or email"/>
                    <field name="go" label="Search" input="submit"/>
                </fields>
            </form>

            <!-- ======================================================
                 6. component —— components
                 name is required; <data> is optional, its child element names
                 are the data keys, and values support interpolation
                 ====================================================== -->

            <heading level="2">6. Components</heading>

            <!-- No data: only the component name is passed -->
            <component name="badge"/>

            <!-- card: title / body (body is emitted as written and may contain
                 HTML) -->
            <component name="card">
                <data>
                    <title>Card title</title>
                    <body><![CDATA[Card body, may contain <em>HTML</em> fragments.]]></body>
                </data>
            </component>

            <!-- button: text / href (optional; a <button> is rendered when it
                 is omitted) / type -->
            <component name="button">
                <data>
                    <text>Edit {{ user.name }}</text>
                    <href>/users/{{ user.id }}/edit</href>
                    <type>primary</type>
                </data>
            </component>

            <!-- alert: type (info/success/warning/danger, default info) / text -->
            <component name="alert">
                <data>
                    <type>warning</type>
                    <text>Your account expires in {{ user.daysLeft }} days.</text>
                </data>
            </component>

            <!-- data values support interpolation; escaping is decided by the
                 component template (here alert's e()) -->
            <component name="alert">
                <data>
                    <type>success</type>
                    <text>Saved {{ user.messageCount }} settings.</text>
                </data>
            </component>

            <!-- my-card: a custom component shipped with this example, its file
                 is examples/components/my-card.php. The only difference from a
                 built-in component is that it is not distributed inside the
                 package. See the "Custom components" appendix at the end. -->
            <component name="my-card">
                <data>
                    <title>Custom component · {{ user.name }}</title>
                    <body><![CDATA[The body is emitted by the component template with raw(), so <em>HTML</em> fragments can go here.]]></body>
                </data>
            </component>

            <!-- ======================================================
                 7. el / attribute passthrough / attr —— front-end
                    framework integration
                 <el> is a generic container; framework directives are emitted
                 verbatim onto the tag; names XML cannot spell (@-prefixed) use
                 <attr>
                 ====================================================== -->

            <heading level="2">7. Front-end framework integration</heading>

            <!-- Passthrough attributes: directive names with a colon, the
                 x- / v- / hx- / data- prefixes, and class/id/style -->
            <el tag="ul" class="list" data-controller="menu">
                <each items="users" as="member">
                    <body>
                        <!-- Passthrough values support interpolation too: the
                             literal part is escaped first, then the path is
                             substituted -->
                        <el tag="li" data-id="{{ member.id }}" x-on:click="select($el)">
                            <text>{{ member.name }}</text>
                        </el>
                    </body>
                </each>
            </el>

            <!-- __event is the readable spelling of @event: XML attribute
                 names cannot contain '@' -->
            <el tag="div" x-data="{ open: false }" class="panel" __click="open = ! open">
                <attr name=":class" value="open &amp;&amp; 'open'"/>
                <text>Click to toggle</text>
            </el>

            <!-- Names the mapping does not cover (or a literal __xxx that must
                 be kept) use <attr>; the name is emitted verbatim -->
            <el tag="span" class="tag">
                <attr name="@mouseenter" value="hover = true"/>
                <attr name="__literal" value="untouched"/>
                <text>Hover</text>
            </el>

            <!-- Form fields and links accept passthrough attributes too -->
            <form action="/users/search" method="get" class="search" x-on:submit.prevent="submit()">
                <fields>
                    <field name="q" label="Keyword" input="text" placeholder="Name or email"
                           x-model.debounce.500ms="kw"/>
                    <field name="go" label="Search" input="submit"/>
                </fields>
            </form>

        </section>
    </sections>
</page>

<!--
  ==================================================================
  Appendix: the standalone (layout-less) page form
  ==================================================================

  layout and body are mutually exclusive: without a layout, the page content
  lives directly under <body>. The <page> title attribute is then ignored (with
  a warning), because a standalone page has no layout to inject a title section
  into.

      <?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
      <page>
          <body>
              <heading level="2">Standalone page</heading>
              <text>Hello, {{ user.name }}.</text>
              <each items="users" as="user">
                  <body>
                      <text>{{ user.name }}</text>
                  </body>
              </each>
          </body>
      </page>


  ==================================================================
  Appendix: custom components
  ==================================================================

  my-card in section 6 above is a custom component: its file is
  examples/components/my-card.php, referenced in the page with name="my-card".
  No registration is needed — just add its directory to the template search
  path.

  Writing your own component takes three steps:

  1) Write the component file. A component is an ordinary miGears Template file
     (.php or .tpl.php). In .tpl.php, ## $x ## is escaped output and
     ### $x ### is literal output (and produces an extra compiled cache file):

      // components/my-card.php
      <div class="my-card">
          <h3><?= $this->e($title ?? '') ?></h3>
          <div><?= $this->raw((string) ($body ?? '')) ?></div>
      </div>

  2) Make its directory findable. Directories added later are searched first,
     so dropping a same-named file into a later-registered directory overrides
     a built-in component (theme overriding):

      $tpl->addPath(__DIR__ . '/components');

  3) Reference it by name in the page:

      <component name="my-card">
          <data>
              <title>{{ user.name }}</title>
              <body><![CDATA[Body text, may contain <em>HTML</em>.]]></body>
          </data>
      </component>

  Key points:
    · The name is a path relative to some registered path, so subdirectories
      work directly: name="admin/table" hits <path>/admin/table.php. The same
      file gets a different name under a different base path: registering the
      components/ directory makes it card; registering the package root makes
      it components/card.
    · Each data key becomes a local variable inside the component; values are
      strings only, and the page's other variables do not leak in.
    · Data values arrive unescaped; whether they are escaped depends on the
      component template: use $this->e() for text and $this->raw() for trusted
      HTML. Pre-escaping on the page side would double-escape.
    · <component> itself emits no tag, so it cannot carry class and other
      attributes; wrap it in <el> when outer attributes are needed.
    · A missing component is not an error at compile time — it only throws a
      Component not found: <name> exception at render time.
-->